{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l31eqrx0","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"magnetism","chapterGroup":"electricity","topic":"magnetic-properties-of-matter","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pin-the-graph-below-the-resistance-r-of-a-superconductor-jee-advanced-physics-magnetism-kgreogwrqvei0ubd","content":"<p>In the graph below, the resistance R of a superconductor is shown as a friction of its temperature T for two different magnetic fields B<sub>1</sub> (solid line) and B<sub>2</sub> (dashed line). If B<sub>2</sub> is larger than B<sub>1</sub> which of the following graphs shows the correct variation of R with T in these fields?</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31trwzc/6a2779ca-6f15-46c5-9059-137194e78510/7dd07a90-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31trwzd.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l31trwzc/6a2779ca-6f15-46c5-9059-137194e78510/7dd07a90-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31trwzd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Magnetism Question 19 English Option 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31trwzc/6a2779ca-6f15-46c5-9059-137194e78510/7dd07a90-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31trwzd.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31trwzc/6a2779ca-6f15-46c5-9059-137194e78510/7dd07a90-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31trwzd.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31trwzc/6a2779ca-6f15-46c5-9059-137194e78510/7dd07a90-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31trwzd.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31trwzc/6a2779ca-6f15-46c5-9059-137194e78510/7dd07a90-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31trwzd.png?format=png 1500w, https://app