bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Magnetism Question 19 English Option 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l31tv21e/bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l31tv21e/bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l31tv21e/bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l31tv21e/bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l31tv21e/bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l31tv21e/bc9b4912-8379-49dc-9ff8-281a0bbb41e9/d525cf20-d14b-11ec-a5f4-6d60b89817cd/file-1l31tv21f.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>From the given figure, T<sub>c</sub>(B) is a monotonically decreasing function of B. Thus, B<sub>2</sub> > B<sub>1</sub> implies T<sub>c</sub>(B<sub>2</sub>) < T<sub>c</sub>(B<sub>1</sub>). Hence resistance with B<sub>2</sub> will become zero at lower temperature in comparison to B<sub>1</sub>.</p>"}]}